We use final when we are not going to change the variable at all.
When we initialize a private final field we just defend the field to be changed by us since its not public
we just making changes. Inside the class.
If we have a final reference then we can change the reference content but we can't change the reference itself
when we have a final array we change the array content but we can't point on different array.

mutable - a thing that we can change (like the reference content)
immutable - a thing that can't be changed (like the reference himself)